{
  "title": "Tons of Skills \u2014 Claude Code Plugins Marketplace \u2014 marketplace (2,232\u2605)",
  "content": "Project: Tons of Skills \u2014 Claude Code Plugins Marketplace\nDomain: marketplace | Scale: medium | Stars: 2,232\nProblem: Developers using Claude Code lack a centralized, curated marketplace to discover and install reusable plugins, skills, and AI agents. This project provides an open-source registry with a CLI package manager (ccpi) to search, install, and manage 425+ plugins and 2,810+ skills for Claude Code.\nTarget users: Software developers using Claude Code, DevOps engineers automating workflows with AI, AI/LLM practitioners building agent-based tooling, Plugin and skill contributors to the open-source ecosystem\nCore features: CLI package manager (ccpi) for searching, installing, and updating plugins; Curated marketplace of 425+ plugins and 2,810+ skills for Claude Code; Web marketplace UI at tonsofskills.com for browsing and discovery; 200 pre-built AI agents ready to deploy; MCP (Model Context Protocol) server support for plugin execution; Downloadable plugin bundle packages (cowork zips); Automated daily npm download metrics tracking via GitHub Actions; Killer Skill of the Week spotlight with automated README rendering\nIntegrations: Anthropic Claude Code, npm / pnpm registry, GitHub Actions (CI/CD, metrics updates), Kobiton real-device cloud (mobile testing MCP), OpenBB Terminal, Skyvern AI, Nixtla (sponsor/integration), tonsofskills.com (hosted marketplace)\nTech stack: Astro (marketplace web UI) + Python / Node.js (plugin servers, MCP servers, CLI scripts) + GitHub Actions, npm registry, pnpm monorepo\nKey libraries: pnpm workspaces, js-yaml, archiver, eslint, prettier, husky, lint-staged, commitlint, TypeScript\nArchitecture: monolith\nDesign lessons:\n- Monorepo structure with pnpm workspaces allows managing 400+ plugin packages and a CLI tool under a single version-controlled repository with shared tooling.\n- Automated scripts (sync-marketplace, generate-readme-toc, update-metrics) keep the README, marketplace JSON, and download stats consistent without manual intervention, essential at this catalog scale.\n- MCP (Model Context Protocol) is used as the plugin execution interface, decoupling plugin logic from Claude Code's core and enabling third-party contributors to publish independently via npm.\n- A companion CLI (ccpi) published to npm mirrors the plugin install experience of traditional package managers, lowering the barrier to adoption for developer-tool audiences.",
